### 15:10–16:00 · Viết tài liệu

`docs/notifications.md`:

```markdown
# Notification strategy

## What I send
One reminder per meal slot, only if the user hasn't logged that meal, only
within their configured window, and never during their quiet hours.

## What I deliberately don't send
- Streak-break warnings. They create guilt, and guilt makes people delete
  the app rather than open it.
- "We miss you" re-engagement pushes. If someone stopped using a food diary,
  a notification isn't what brings them back.
- Anything marketing-shaped. This app has one job.

## Permission timing
Never on launch. The system dialog on iOS only appears once, so I show my own
explainer when the user turns reminders on, and only trigger the OS prompt if
they say yes. If they decline mine, I can ask again later — if they decline
the OS one, I can't.

## What I measure
Delivery rate, open rate, action rate, and opt-out rate. Opt-out is the one I
watch hardest. A high open rate with a rising opt-out rate means I'm spending
trust for short-term engagement, and that trade never pays back — once someone
turns notifications off, there's no way to ask again.
```

